# Cloudflare Pages _headers
#
# Content Security Policy — ENFORCING as of 2026-08-15.
#
# Verified before enforcing: the static resource graph (headless Chrome against
# a local build, policy applied as a real header) and the HLS/video path (real
# browser, real playback — this is what caught the jsdelivr dependency below).
#
# 📝 RESOLVED — Cloudflare JS Detections vs. this policy (14–15 Aug 2026).
# Kept because the reasoning still applies if JS Detections is ever re-enabled.
#
# Super Bot Fight Mode's "JS Detections" makes Cloudflare inject a per-request
# inline bootstrap for /cdn-cgi/challenge-platform/scripts/jsd/main.js. Its
# content differs on every request, so it cannot be allowed by hash; a static
# _headers file cannot issue a per-request nonce; and 'unsafe-inline' would
# defeat the policy. A strict script-src and JS Detections are therefore
# mutually exclusive — there is no configuration of this file that satisfies
# both.
#
# Enabled 2026-08-14, which left JS Detections non-functional once the policy
# began enforcing. Rather than loosen script-src, JS Detections was switched
# OFF on 2026-08-15 (Cloudflare dashboard → Security → Settings — NOT
# Security → Bots). Confirmed still off 2026-08-23. Nothing is outstanding,
# and the contact form was tested working both before and after: its
# first-line defence is the Worker's honeypot + email validation, not this.
#
# ⚠️ If JS Detections is ever switched back on, the conflict returns in full
# and cannot be fixed from this file. The remedies are a WAF skip rule on the
# affected path, or leaving it off. The rest of Super Bot Fight Mode
# (Definitely automated → Block, Verified bots → Allow) is unaffected either
# way; the Likely automated tier does not exist on this Pro zone.
#
# Derived from an audit of every subresource the site actually loads
# (see the vault: Sites/donaldjenkins.com/CSP audit and proposal.md).
# Notes on the non-obvious directives:
#   style-src   'unsafe-inline' is required by the inline style="" attribute in
#               shortcodes/contactform.html and by Vidstack's runtime styling.
#               cdnjs is the normalize.min.css that only layouts/404.html loads.
#   img-src     data: is used by background SVGs in the compiled CSS.
#               assets.via.dj serves the 404 illustration and video thumbnails.
#   media-src   blob: is required for HLS playback via Media Source Extensions.
#   worker-src  blob: is required by hls.js, which demuxes in a Web Worker.
#   form-action MUST include the contact-form Worker — the form posts directly
#               to it, so a bare 'self' here silently breaks /contact.
#   script-src  'self' covers the Plausible script, which is proxied through
#               this origin at /guests/hurrah/. Inline JSON-LD is a data block,
#               not an executed script, so it needs no allowance.
#               cdn.jsdelivr.net WAS required here until 2026-08-16: vidstack's
#               dist hardcodes `cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/hls.js@^1.0.0/dist/
#               hls.min.js` and fetched it at runtime on any page with a video.
#               No template referenced it, so it was invisible to source
#               analysis and was caught only by loading a video page.
#               hls.js is now SELF-HOSTED — mounted from node_modules in
#               config.toml and pointed at by static/js/vidstack-hls.js — so
#               script-src is back to a bare 'self'. ⚠️ If video ever breaks
#               with a blocked cdn.jsdelivr.net script, that shim has stopped
#               working; fix the shim rather than re-adding the allowance.

# Permissions-Policy — added 2026-08-16 (flagged as missing by securityheaders.com).
# Denies browser features the site has no use for. The three (self) entries are
# deliberate, NOT oversights: the video player is Vidstack (custom element
# <media-player>, playing HLS hosted on Cloudflare Stream), and denying
# fullscreen or picture-in-picture outright would break its controls on the 18
# articles that carry a video shortcode. Features not listed keep the browser
# default. encrypted-media is intentionally omitted — the Cloudflare Stream
# videos are not DRM-protected, but the default is permissive enough if that
# ever changes.

/*
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=(), autoplay=(self), fullscreen=(self), picture-in-picture=(self)
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; img-src 'self' data: https://assets.via.dj https://*.cloudflarestream.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://*.cloudflarestream.com; media-src 'self' blob: https://*.cloudflarestream.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; form-action 'self' https://donaldjenkins-contactform.policymakr.workers.dev; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cache lifetimes (added 2026-08-15)
#
# Cloudflare Pages' default for static assets is
# `public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate` — 4 hours, then a conditional
# request answered 304. The rules below replace that on the paths where a
# longer life is safe. Rules are additive: the /* block above contributes the
# CSP, these contribute Cache-Control, and both apply.
#
# ⚠️ The dividing line is FINGERPRINTING, and it is the only thing that makes
# `immutable` safe. Hugo's `fingerprint` puts a content hash in the filename
# (styles.min.<hash>.css), so changing the file changes its URL and no cache
# can serve a stale copy. Assets WITHOUT a hash in the name keep a stable URL
# forever, so a long max-age means an edit stays invisible for that long.
# Never add `immutable` to an unfingerprinted path.
#
# HTML is deliberately untouched: it keeps Pages' `max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# so a deploy is visible immediately. That is what makes the rest safe — the
# freshly-fetched HTML always names the current hashed CSS.

# Content-hashed by Hugo. Safe to cache for a year and never revalidate.
/css/styles.min.*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# NOT fingerprinted — stable filenames, so no `immutable` and no year.
# 30 days trades a small staleness window for dropping the 4-hourly
# revalidation round-trip. logo.svg is the only one of these on every page.
# ⚠️ To force an update inside the window, RENAME the file (and its
# references); re-uploading under the same name will not reach warm caches.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

# Only figtree.woff2, and only the 404 page loads it.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
